.TH KINTSUGI-BRANDING 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-branding \- the Kintsugi identity kit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi branding
wordmark
.br
.B kintsugi branding
sigil
.br
.B kintsugi branding
palette
.br
.B kintsugi branding
export
.I dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the Kintsugi identity in the terminal, or export it as SVG assets.
The art and the colours come from the same tables the TUI draws from, so an
exported asset cannot disagree with what the terminal renders.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP "\fBwordmark\fR" 14
Print the block KINTSUGI wordmark at its native 19 columns, shaded across the heat
ramp from glow at the left to accent-deep at the right.
.IP "\fBsigil\fR" 14
Print the compact anvil mark: 6 rows by 13 columns, spark above the anvil.
.IP "\fBpalette\fR" 14
Print every design token with its name, hex value, 256-colour fallback and
16-colour fallback, followed by a live swatch row. The output is honest about
the active profile; under NO_COLOR, TERM=dumb or a non-terminal stdout it is
plain text with no escape sequences.
.IP "\fBexport\fR \fIdir\fR" 14
Write
.IR wordmark.svg ,
.I sigil.svg
and
.I palette.svg
into
.IR dir ,
creating it if needed. Each glyph is one rect on a cell grid inside a
self-contained document with a viewBox and a background.
.SH EXAMPLES
Draw the wordmark:
.PP
  $ kintsugi branding wordmark
.PP
Inspect the palette for this terminal:
.PP
  $ kintsugi branding palette
.PP
Write the asset kit:
.PP
  $ kintsugi branding export branding/
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1)